abstract: >
  The Classical Regge Growth (CRG) conjecture is well-defined at n=4 but its generalization to
  n>=5 particles is genuinely ambiguous, with no definition in the literature. Using the
  five-photon operator basis of a companion note (arXiv/Zenodo: 10.5281/zenodo.22819347), this
  note constructs three qualitatively distinct families of n=5 Regge trajectories and shows that
  the combined kernel of degree-11 candidates satisfying the conjectured bound across all three
  families is exactly {0}, on the complete 16-dimensional space explored. States this as an open
  problem rather than a resolved negative result.
